    {
      "id": "tokoro-before-lunch",
      "jlpt": 4,
      "target": "tokoro-before",
      "relationship": "tokoro-action-stages",
      "prompt": "昼ご飯がテーブルにそろいました。食事はまだ始めていません。箸（はし）を持って、これから昼ご飯を____ところです。",
      "translation": "Use 食べる (たべる, eat): dictionary, ている or た form; contractions accepted. Lunch is on the table, but I have not started the meal. With chopsticks in hand, I am just about to eat lunch.",
      "evidence": "The meal has not begun, but the food and chopsticks are ready and これから places its start immediately ahead.",
      "explanation": "食べるところです locates the speaker just before starting the meal. The dictionary form attaches directly to ところ, even though the sentence ends politely with です. This is a controlled choice of verb form before the printed ところ, not a request for any possible expression of intention.",
      "answer": "tokoro-before",
      "acceptedAnswers": [
        "食べる",
        "たべる"
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "tokoro-before",
          "label": "食べる",
          "rationale": "Places eating just ahead, matching the meal that is ready but not yet begun."
        },
        {
          "id": "tokoro-during",
          "label": "食べている",
          "rationale": "Would put the speaker in the middle of eating, contrary to 食事はまだ始めていません."
        },
        {
          "id": "tokoro-after",
          "label": "食べた",
          "rationale": "Would present the meal as just eaten, not about to begin."
        }
      ],
